                <pb facs="0170" n="100" xml:id="pg100"/>

                <head>No. 47.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Logan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 2,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Logan is informed that the action of Mr. Partridge, as reported by Mr. Logan,
                    is unauthorized, and that he has been directed to make explanations; that
                    instructions suggesting the recognition of the government of Calderon have been
                    sent by mail.</p>
                <p>Tarapaca to be ceded to Chili by Peru. United States will agree to arbitrate in
                    the event that Chili is to receive any further indemnity.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
